---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LinkBar from "../components/LinkBar.astro";
import BibtexBlock from "../components/BibtexBlock.astro";
import MethodologyFigure from "../components/MethodologyFigure.astro";
import PrevalenceChart from "../components/PrevalenceChart.astro";
import { authors, affiliations, paper } from "../data/paper";
---
<BaseLayout title={paper.title}>
  <span class="venue-badge">{paper.venue}</span>
  <h1>{paper.title}</h1>

  <p class="authors">
    {authors.map((author, i) => (
      <>
        <span>{author.name}<sup>{author.affiliation === "chula" ? "†" : "‡"}{author.corresponding ? "*" : ""}</sup></span>
        {i < authors.length - 1 ? ", " : ""}
      </>
    ))}
  </p>
  <p class="affiliations">
    <sup>†</sup> {affiliations.chula} &nbsp;&nbsp; <sup>‡</sup> {affiliations.google}
  </p>

  <LinkBar />

  <p class="tldr">
    <strong>TL;DR:</strong> Since 2022, NLP conferences require every paper to
    disclose its own limitations — creating a huge, unanalyzed archive of
    researchers admitting what's wrong with their own work. We built a
    human-AI pipeline (validated against expert annotators) to categorize
    over 16,000 of these disclosures, and found that what researchers report
    barely varies by research area — a surprisingly uniform picture of how
    the field talks about its own shortcomings.
  </p>

  <h2>Abstract</h2>
  <p>{paper.abstract}</p>

  <h2>Methodology</h2>
  <p>
    A human-AI pipeline alternates between an LLM proposing codes for each
    sentence and a researcher reviewing any genuinely new category it
    surfaces. Click a stage to see how it works, with a real worked example:
  </p>
  <MethodologyFigure />
  <p class="section-cta">
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}methodology`}>Full methodology walkthrough &rarr;</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Dataset</h2>
  <p>
    This site's <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}explore`}>explorer</a> covers
    the <strong>16,047-paper LLM-coded dataset</strong> — every ACL/EMNLP main and
    Findings paper (2020–2025) with a Limitations section, coded with sentence-level
    evidence spans and justifications.
  </p>

  <h3>Inter-annotator agreement</h3>
  <p>
    To make sure the LLM's coding is trustworthy, it was validated against a
    separate <strong>150-paper reference set</strong> independently coded by
    four expert human annotators (that reference set isn't separately
    browsable here, since a few of its papers come from small workshop
    tracks outside this site's ACL/EMNLP main+Findings scope).
  </p>
  <p class="iaa-numbers">
    <span class="badge badge-human">Human annotators only</span>
    <strong>α = 0.644</strong>
    <span class="iaa-arrow">&rarr;</span>
    <span class="badge badge-llm">+ LLM as a coder</span>
    <strong>α = 0.647</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Agreement barely changes when the LLM is added as a fifth coder — the
    basis for treating its coding of the remaining ~16,000 papers as
    reliable.
  </p>
  <p class="section-cta">
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}results`}>See the full per-code agreement breakdown &rarr;</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Results</h2>
  <p>Which limitations come up most often across the 16,047 LLM-coded papers:</p>
  <PrevalenceChart />
  <p class="section-cta">
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}results`}>Full results: temporal trends &amp; the homogeneity finding &rarr;</a>
  </p>

  <BibtexBlock />

  <p class="cta">
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}explore`}>Explore the dataset &rarr;</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .venue-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: white;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  h1 { margin-top: 0.25rem; }
  .authors { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .affiliations { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .tldr {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .iaa-numbers {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .iaa-arrow { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .section-cta { font-weight: 600; }
  .cta { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; }
</style>
